== Switching to JSSE Connector ==

=== Creating password file ===

Store the password for the PKCS #12 files into a file:

<pre>
$ echo Secret.123 > /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.pwd
$ chown pkiuser.pkiuser /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.pwd
$ chmod 0660 /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.pwd
</pre>

=== Exporting SSL server certificate ===

Export the SSL server certificate with the following command:

<pre>
$ pki-server cert-export \
    sslserver \
    --instance "pki-tomcat" \
    --pkcs12-file /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.p12 \
    --pkcs12-password-file /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.pwd \
    --cert-encryption "PBE/SHA1/RC2-40" \
    --key-encryption "PBE/SHA1/DES3/CBC"
</pre>

Alternatively, the SSL server certificate can be exported with the following command:

<pre>
$ pk12util \
    -n sslserver \
    -d /var/lib/pki/pki-tomcat/alias \
    -k Secret.123 \
    -o /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.p12 \
    -w /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.pwd
</pre>

Then configure the file permission as follows:

<pre>
$ chown pkiuser.pkiuser /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.p12
$ chmod 0660 /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.p12
</pre>

=== Configuring JSSE connector ===

To configure JSSE connector:

<pre>
$ pki-server http-connector-mod Secure \
    --type JSSE \
    --keystore-file /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.p12 \
    --keystore-password-file /etc/pki/pki-tomcat/keystore.pwd
